Debug aid (NOT a fix): per-draw / per-resolve GPU logging, and draw skipping

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk),
            on top of the regular patches 0001-0003 (it touches the same
            lines of draw.cpp as 0003, so apply those first)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/debug/0100-gpu-draw-resolve-diag.patch
Remove with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply -R ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/debug/0100-gpu-draw-resolve-diag.patch
Status:     local debugging tool. Lives in debug/ so the normal
            `git apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/*.patch` step skips it.
            Rebuild the SDK (RelWithDebInfo install) and the game after
            applying or removing it.

WHAT IT'S FOR
  Chasing "the picture is wrong/black" bugs when there's no frame debugger
  (no RenderDoc on this machine, and ReXGlue dropped Xenia's GPU tracer).
  It writes one log line per GPU draw and per resolve (EDRAM -> RAM copy),
  but only for the frames you pick, so logs stay readable.

HOW TO USE IT (environment variables, read once at startup)
  CRASHMOM_DIAG_FRAMES="15000,20000"
      Milliseconds since the GPU plugin loaded (about process start). At the
      first swap after each time, every draw and resolve until the next swap
      is logged:
        DRAW-DIAG frame N begins (t=...)
        DRAW-DIAG draw prim= idx= VS=<ucode hash> PS=<hash|none> surf pitch=
                  msaa= rt0 base= fmt= depth base= winoff= COLOR_MASK=
                  BLEND0= COLORCONTROL= DEPTHCONTROL= tex_mask=
        DRAW-DIAG   texN addr= fmt= WxH tiled= ...    (each bound texture)
        RESOLVE-DIAG ok|EMPTY verts=... raw=... scissor=... -> [x0,x1)x[y0,y1)
                  src=(0-3 color RT, 4 depth) dest=0x... fmt= ...
        DRAW-DIAG swap frontbuffer=0x... (end of logged frame)
      Pair with --debug_capture_dir (src/debug_frame_capture.h) to see the
      picture of the same moment.
  CRASHMOM_DIAG_SKIP="72,12"
      Skip triangle-list draws that use the palette pixel shader
      28DB7E4D9D1CB9CF with these index counts (was used to rule out the
      title screen's electricity draws). Edit the hash for other shaders.
  CRASHMOM_DIAG_SKIP_DEPTHONLY=1
      Skip depth-only rectangle-list draws on a 640-wide 4x MSAA surface.
      Proved that the game's clears right before the final copy are what
      blank the title screen in the FBO render-target path (findings/06).

WHERE (src/graphics/util/draw.cpp, src/graphics/vulkan/command_processor.cpp)
  draw.cpp: GetResolveInfo() logs the resolve rectangle before and after the
  scissor clamp (the "Resolve region is empty" investigation). The shared
  flag g_crashmom_diag_frame says whether the current frame is logged.
  command_processor.cpp: IssueSwap() starts/ends logged frames;
  IssueDraw() logs the draw + textures and applies the skips.

HOW WE USED IT: docs/findings/06-black-screens-render-target-path.md

